The find path's lane mask selects the value lanes, not the key lanes.

A bucket is four 16-byte {k, v} pairs, so as eight qwords the line is
k0 v0 k1 v1 k2 v2 k3 v3 -- keys on the even lanes. 0b10101010 selects
lanes 1,3,5,7, i.e. the values, so the search key is compared against
stored MAC addresses and every lookup misses. The `offset + 1` two lines
later in dramblast.c is only coherent for an even offset, so the two
disagree on their face; upstream DRAMHiT uses 0b01010101 over the
identical layout (kvtypes.hpp:643).

Verified by l2fwd/test_dramblast_find.c: 0 of 64 hits before, 64 of 64
correct after. Worth 17.3 TSC ticks/packet of the 52.9 measured, because
a path that misses on every packet also inserts on every packet.
See docs/INVESTIGATION.md section 5.26.

--- a/l2fwd/libsashstore/dramblast.h
+++ b/l2fwd/libsashstore/dramblast.h
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
 #define DRAMBLAST_MAX_BURST 64
 // make multiple of 4.
 #define DRAMBLAST_BUCKET_IDX_MASK ~0x3
-#define DRAMBLAST_SIMD_KEY_MASK 0b10101010
+#define DRAMBLAST_SIMD_KEY_MASK 0b01010101
 extern int dramblast_queue_depth;  /* prefetch pipeline depth, power of two */
 extern int dramblast_alloc_pairs; /* -1 hoisted, 0 as shipped, n extra pairs */
 void dramblast_init(void);
